      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T08:24:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s possible to do this way but we are using NEW_IMG so far because it tells/determines what\u0027s needed for it. We have node property called `preserve`, which tells a section should be preserved or not. If it\u0027s set to false it won\u0027t do the preserve.\n\nOne case this change could break is, if the CBI portion has `preserve` flag set false in CUR_IMG and set to true in NEW_IMG.  The general expectation is it needs to preserve or get the CBI data from CUR_IMG, but it won\u0027t with this change\n\nOther case would be, If CUR_IMG marked CBI as preserve, but in NEW_IMG it\u0027s marked as don\u0027t preserve and we have new CBI data in NEW_IMG, we could only flash it using --no_preserve tag to avoid preserving. But --no_preserve should not be required in this case as per device tree configuration in NEW_IMG\n\nWe need to use --no_preserve until we don\u0027t have CBI data present in the CUR_IMG. Without `no_preserve` it fails which also works as alert that the CBI section is not in-place. Generally --no_preserve is meant for factory use case to put initial CBI into device, similar to flashing EEPROM at factory, normally dev won\u0027t need this flag.\n\nThe flashing won\u0027t fail in the following case but it\u0027s expected to, CUR_IMG don\u0027t have CBI, but NEW_IMG (with `preserve` flag set to true) is expecting to get the CBI from CUR_IMG\n\nIt\u0027s also bit complicated for a new user to understand if the behavior relies on old image properties, instead of new image properties",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f46a5f88_2fdaaefb",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1190764
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T09:03:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "using NEW_IMG doesn\u0027t make sense because that ignores the preserve flag\nin the existing image. more importantly, the implemented logic detects\na false failure when the existing image does not have a CBI region.\n\n`The general expectation is it needs to preserve or get the CBI data from CUR_IMG`\nthe preserve flag that needs to be respected is the one that describes\nthe bits at risk. using the preserved flag from the new image to infer\nthat bits in the old image should be preserved is strange. i don\u0027t\nthink setting the preserve bit in the new image should have precedent\nover the preserve bit in the old image. if we need to \"invalidate\"\nthe preserve setting in the old image, we should use the --no_preserve\nflag.\n\nwhat\u0027s complicated is that flash_ec now requires special attention to\ntransition a system from a flashmap without CBI to one with CBI and that\u0027s\nentirely avoidable.",
      "parentUuid": "4203e0c4_454cce61",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af35c58a_cdcc83af",
        "filename": "util/flash_ec",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1757,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T09:37:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t use `no_preserve` often, it\u0027s only meant for first flash of CBI in EC flash. \n\nThe devices generally come with CBI in EC flash from factory. Consider `no_preserve` will not be used by us, until CBI is corrupted that came from factory\n\nNormally a EC dev won\u0027t face the case that is addressed here AFAIK i.e, the flash failing because CBI is not present in OLD_IMG, but the NEW_IMG trying to preserve it\n\nThe behavior of property `preserve` is inspired from binman: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/third_party/u-boot/+/4500973\n\nActually what we meant by (or my understanding of) preserve is, we won\u0027t use the sections that are marked `preserve`(in image with updates) from new binary, while updating all sections on flash. we continue using current version of the preserve sections, while others get updated\n\nBut in flash_ec case, we can\u0027t do flashing section wise, if it was possible we would have skipped flashing those sections based on NEW_IMG `preserve\u0027 flags, so we are copying the sections that marked as `preserve` in NEW_IMG from OLD_IMG, keeping other sections as it is in NEW_IMG\n\nIf I understood it correctly, I think the error coming up at flashing process when trying to preserve some sections from CUR_IMG which don\u0027t have them, is a valid error, cause it tells me the valid data not available in earlier version, instead of silently skipping copying, booting up and failing later with error \"Invalid CBI data\"",
      "parentUuid": "f46a5f88_2fdaaefb",
      "revId": "5a9ee73aac97b76e3a708b87151e4f33ae0d6c15",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
